# Round F: static-phase probe responsiveness plus dense thread sampling of 80..130 s. The prefix
# (lsprobe anchors, stop-mode watcher, drag at about 91 s, home at about 101 s) is byte-identical
# to rc.jobs.freeze so the round stays comparable with C/D/E; the changes are the periodic grid
# count, eleven single-shot dumpers on a 5 s grid over 80..130 s, and the probe tail on rwtouch.
#
#   one stop-mode framewatch with MAX_DUMPS 0, which only reports "still" and never takes a slot;
#   one periodic framewatch, 30 dumps 20 s apart, which now covers the whole 420 s round;
#   eleven periodic framewatch instances with --count 1, firing once each at 80,85,...,130 s
#   after their own start (all start within milliseconds of boot, so the grid is round-relative);
#   rwtouch probes at about 146/161/176/191/206/221 s, each readable three independent ways:
#   still-count reset, swap-id growth, and the 3 s screenshot grid's hash and tier changes.
#
# init waits for each line, so every background line ends with & and goes before rwtouch.
/redwood/bin/lsprobe 60 &
/redwood/bin/lsprobe 300 &
/redwood/bin/framewatch 5 0 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 20 --count 30 SpringBoard backboardd &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 80 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 85 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 90 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 95 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 100 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 105 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 110 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 115 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 120 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 125 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/framewatch --every 130 --count 1 backboardd SpringBoard &
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 90 swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 250 wait 10 button home wait 45 button lock wait 15 button lock wait 15 button volup wait 15 swipe 0.5 0.02 0.5 0.5 400 wait 15 swipe 0.5 0.985 0.5 0.3 250 wait 15 tap 0.5 0.92 wait 20
# framewatch has no start delay, and init starts each line when the previous one returns, so this
# watcher starts when the rwtouch above finishes, at about 241 s in this file (the probe tail
# runs 140 s; rc.jobs.freeze ends its rwtouch 90 s earlier and puts this watcher at about 150 s).
# The threshold is 2 s and there are six dumps. The periodic holes it was written for measure 3 s
# every 15 s starting at rel 30-34 s in round-relative seconds; the "about 180 s" that earlier
# versions of this comment carried was the old freeze round's device monotonic clock, whose zero
# sits 146.7 s before that round's own start, and 180 - 146.7 = 33.3 matches the measured hole
# starts 33.8 (freeze), 31.4 (C), 30.3 (D). A 5 s threshold never fires inside a 3 s hole, and
# starting late keeps the boot's own frameless stretch from spending the dumps on it. In this
# round the six dumps land after the whole probe sequence, sampling the deep static phase.
/redwood/bin/framewatch 2 6 backboardd SpringBoard
